From: LightHost Maintainers <support@linkease.com>
Subject: [PATCH] storage/lvm: settle activation before filesystem mount

OpenWrt dispatches device-mapper remove events asynchronously. A remove event
from a previous deactivation can therefore arrive after the same dm-N name has
been reused by a subsequent activation. block hotplug then detaches the new
mount by device name while Incus is preparing an idmapped container rootfs.

Wait after a real filesystem-volume activation and before exposing a new mount.
This lets stale remove events drain while there is no filesystem mount for them
to detach. Already-active volumes do not pay the delay.

--- a/internal/server/storage/drivers/driver_lvm_volumes.go
+++ b/internal/server/storage/drivers/driver_lvm_volumes.go
@@ -11,6 +11,7 @@ import (
 	"os/exec"
 	"path/filepath"
 	"strings"
+	"time"
 
 	"golang.org/x/sys/unix"
 
@@ -997,6 +998,14 @@ func (d *lvm) MountVolume(vol Volume, op
 		return err
 	}
 
+	// OpenWrt handles device-mapper remove events asynchronously. If a recently
+	// deactivated dm-N name is reused, a stale remove event can detach a new
+	// filesystem mount. Let those events drain before the mount becomes visible.
+	// Volumes that were already active don't need the stabilization window.
+	if activated && vol.contentType == ContentTypeFS {
+		time.Sleep(2 * time.Second)
+	}
+
 	if activated {
 		reverter.Add(func() { _, _ = d.deactivateVolume(vol) })
 	}
